00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:35.123
to make a delivery.

00:12:35.123 --> 00:12:37.480
This is because gangs
have exclusive control

00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:39.110
over some part of the territory.

00:12:39.110 --> 00:12:40.530
So the trucks,

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:42.690
once they go cannot
choose which gang to pay

00:12:42.690 --> 00:12:44.500
when they make a delivery.

00:12:44.500 --> 00:12:46.830
So basically the gangs
compete over territory,

00:12:46.830 --> 00:12:49.153
rather like competing
to provide protection.

00:12:50.849 --> 00:12:52.543
And what happens, yes, Paula.

00:12:53.830 --> 00:12:56.890
- Protection from the other gang.

00:12:56.890 --> 00:12:57.980
- Yeah, exactly.

00:12:57.980 --> 00:12:59.490
Because that's the other bullet

00:12:59.490 --> 00:13:02.280
that you could be
thinking, which is, okay,

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:03.610
you pay me this amount,

00:13:03.610 --> 00:13:05.650
but I protect you for this other gang,

00:13:05.650 --> 00:13:08.883
but that's not how it was at
least not in this context.

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:11.144
- Okay.

00:13:11.144 --> 00:13:12.210
So I had a follow up
question from earlier.

00:13:12.210 --> 00:13:15.910
I wanted to say you explain it
when you showed us the graph

00:13:15.910 --> 00:13:18.350
very early on in the presentation,

00:13:18.350 --> 00:13:19.183
there seems to be

00:13:19.183 --> 00:13:22.460
a lot of variation over
time in extortions.

00:13:22.460 --> 00:13:26.790
And you show us that there
is a huge power max in 2016,

00:13:26.790 --> 00:13:29.210
but there was another
discontinuity that you have marked,

00:13:29.210 --> 00:13:30.900
which was at 2012.

00:13:30.900 --> 00:13:32.730
But in general, after 2012,

00:13:32.730 --> 00:13:34.950
which is the first time
you see throw pain,

00:13:34.950 --> 00:13:37.502
it goes up for a long period
of time and it's erratic,

00:13:37.502 --> 00:13:38.917
but it's quite steady here at some point.

00:13:38.917 --> 00:13:42.820
It's a very sharp increase
before it falls again.

00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:44.340
So if you could just
explain just a little bit,

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:48.270
in addition to these non aggression paths,

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:51.600
what else is a major driver of?

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:53.870
- I will come to this in three slides,

00:13:53.870 --> 00:13:55.460
I think so, to explain to you,

00:13:55.460 --> 00:13:56.913
it was on homicides
actually what I was showing,

00:13:56.913 --> 00:13:59.810
and yes, I can explain you
why there it went down.

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:01.310
It's actually quite important.

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:03.033
- Thank you.

00:14:03.033 --> 00:14:03.866
- Just to finish this.

00:14:03.866 --> 00:14:05.760
So what happens if they decide not to pay?

00:14:05.760 --> 00:14:06.860
No, you can say,

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:10.000
okay, why I cannot pay and that's it.

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:13.170
But actually, the consequence
can be very extreme.

00:14:13.170 --> 00:14:15.210
And this is one news,

00:14:15.210 --> 00:14:16.694
just to put you an
example of what happened

00:14:16.694 --> 00:14:19.580
when one driver that was basically

00:14:19.580 --> 00:14:21.570
distributing bread in a community,

00:14:21.570 --> 00:14:23.520
he said, "I don't want to pay."

00:14:23.520 --> 00:14:26.240
So what happened is they burned their car

00:14:26.240 --> 00:14:28.550
and they turn their car into fire.

00:14:28.550 --> 00:14:29.980
So this can be very extreme.

00:14:29.980 --> 00:14:32.960
So it's not that you
can decide not to pay.

00:14:32.960 --> 00:14:35.120
And most you can decide not to deliver,

00:14:35.120 --> 00:14:36.090
which you would see that

00:14:36.090 --> 00:14:37.780
in the case of our distribution company

00:14:37.780 --> 00:14:39.280
is a bit more difficult for them

00:14:39.280 --> 00:14:41.080
to decide not to deliver to an area.

00:14:42.500 --> 00:14:44.780
And here is where it comes
to your question, Paula.

00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:48.150
So the other thing that I
said I was going to exploit

00:14:48.150 --> 00:14:49.840
is this gang corporation.

00:14:49.840 --> 00:14:53.150
And actually there is a
history in El Salvador,

00:14:53.150 --> 00:14:57.250
the Gang Cooperation, and the
first one, it was a truce,

00:14:57.250 --> 00:15:02.250
which this one in 2012 was
negotiated by the government.

00:15:02.710 --> 00:15:03.820
In March 2012,

00:15:03.820 --> 00:15:06.803
the government sat down with
the leaders of these gangs.

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:09.500
Interestingly, the leaders of these gangs

00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:11.650
are in jail, so they
can know who they are,

00:15:11.650 --> 00:15:13.900
so they can sit down
with them and negotiate.

00:15:14.854 --> 00:15:18.310
And basically, they negotiated
better conditions for gangs

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:20.193
in exchange of reduction in violence.

00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:25.860
The next day that truce was negotiated,

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:28.680
they saw a big decline in homicides.

00:15:28.680 --> 00:15:30.940
This was done under secrecy.

00:15:30.940 --> 00:15:32.830
Nobody knew, it was not that civilians

00:15:32.830 --> 00:15:34.290
knew about this truce.

00:15:34.290 --> 00:15:36.820
What happened is that in 2013,

00:15:36.820 --> 00:15:38.290
they learned about this truce

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:42.110
because there was this
journalistic investigation

00:15:42.110 --> 00:15:44.050
that show and say like, look,

00:15:44.050 --> 00:15:47.340
the government is negotiating
with a terrorist group.

00:15:47.340 --> 00:15:50.120
People didn't like this.

00:15:50.120 --> 00:15:52.590
So the truce was broken

00:15:52.590 --> 00:15:56.360
and they start increasing
also coercion against gangs.

00:15:56.360 --> 00:15:58.915
Gangs also start fighting more for title,

00:15:58.915 --> 00:15:59.748
of course, it was more difficult

00:15:59.748 --> 00:16:01.600
because they increased police.

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:04.000
And that's why you are
seeing this increase.

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:08.430
But at the same time, what
they said is that this truce,

00:16:08.430 --> 00:16:12.320
even though it was broken in 2013,

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:15.110
they set up the grounds
for them to negotiate.

00:16:15.110 --> 00:16:17.260
Basically during the truce,

00:16:17.260 --> 00:16:19.710
what the government used a
lot were religious leaders

00:16:19.710 --> 00:16:21.520
from each communities

00:16:21.520 --> 00:16:25.040
so that they could make
feasible this truce

00:16:25.900 --> 00:16:27.103
to reduce violence.

00:16:28.210 --> 00:16:30.460
And they kept using those to keep meeting

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:33.400
and to try to coordinate.

00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:36.660
And this actually
naturalized in April, 2016

00:16:36.660 --> 00:16:39.762
when the gangs went out and they said

00:16:39.762 --> 00:16:42.750
to journalists and to papers saying,

00:16:42.750 --> 00:16:45.560
with this announcement
that now they agreed

00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:48.073
not to fight and compete
for existing territory.

00:16:49.602 --> 00:16:51.660
And what we see is that this declined,

00:16:51.660 --> 00:16:52.763
and up to today,

00:16:54.637 --> 00:16:56.803
they still are under cooperation.

00:16:57.850 --> 00:16:59.490
And you can see that these homicides

00:16:59.490 --> 00:17:01.843
are still in decline.

00:17:03.180 --> 00:17:07.230
So importantly, when it was
the other truce of 2012,

00:17:07.230 --> 00:17:12.180
many people speculated that
even though homicides decline,

00:17:12.180 --> 00:17:13.810
it increased extortion.

00:17:13.810 --> 00:17:16.850
One theory was that the gang
truce was really an effort

00:17:16.850 --> 00:17:19.500
by larger criminal
interests to grant kind of

00:17:19.500 --> 00:17:21.840
more breathing room to
these criminal operations

00:17:21.840 --> 00:17:23.013
to do their business.

00:17:25.257 --> 00:17:26.819
And we find a lot of anecdotal aliens

00:17:26.819 --> 00:17:29.890
in the field that suggest that for gangs,

00:17:29.890 --> 00:17:31.763
it is costly to kind
of do the truce things

00:17:31.763 --> 00:17:35.500
like to fight the rival
gang and collect extortion.

00:17:35.500 --> 00:17:36.333
And this is mainly

00:17:36.333 --> 00:17:38.379
because they have limited
resources for them.

00:17:38.379 --> 00:17:40.900
It's difficult to recruit people.

00:17:40.900 --> 00:17:44.280
Collecting extortion is
costly and especially costly

00:17:44.280 --> 00:17:45.620
when you are under competition

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:50.537
because you are targeted
by the rival gang to fat.

00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:53.150
And in general,

00:17:53.150 --> 00:17:55.236
there are a lot of
surveys back then in 2013

00:17:55.236 --> 00:17:56.193
where the surveys largely believed

00:17:56.193 --> 00:17:59.050
that the truce benefited the gangs.

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:01.170
And this is one of the potential reasons

00:18:01.170 --> 00:18:02.650
of why this truce in 2012

00:18:02.650 --> 00:18:07.150
was very unpopular because
extortion was still widespread.

00:18:07.150 --> 00:18:09.090
So even though violence declined,

00:18:09.090 --> 00:18:10.580
many of these communities were saying,

00:18:10.580 --> 00:18:13.040
we are still kind of
kidnapped in this situation

00:18:13.040 --> 00:18:15.643
where we have to pay
extortion to these gangs.

00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:21.080
So let me give you now more
details on data descriptive,

00:18:21.080 --> 00:18:23.310
and I will also go more details

00:18:23.310 --> 00:18:25.610
about how this extortion
work in particular

00:18:25.610 --> 00:18:28.690
for the distribution
company than we analyze.

00:18:28.690 --> 00:18:29.523
So what do we have?

00:18:29.523 --> 00:18:33.300
We have here extortion
payment data and sales data

00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:35.660
from this wholesale distribution company

00:18:35.660 --> 00:18:37.563
from 2012 to 2019.

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:41.209
So what can I tell you about this company?

00:18:41.209 --> 00:18:43.120
Is that this is one of the main supplier

00:18:43.120 --> 00:18:45.420
of both consumer products
and pharmaceuticals.

00:18:46.970 --> 00:18:50.570
They buy the goods in
bulk from multinationals,

00:18:50.570 --> 00:18:54.137
and they resell them to local
retailers and pharmacists.

00:18:55.010 --> 00:18:58.046
Importantly, they have
exclusive licensing rights

00:18:58.046 --> 00:19:01.270
with these multinationals
and this allow them

00:19:01.270 --> 00:19:04.080
to be the only distributor
for some of the goods,

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:05.870
especially for pharmaceutical.

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:08.490
This is all what I can
provide you of information

00:19:08.490 --> 00:19:11.330
without breaking the
confidentiality agreement

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:12.500
with the company.

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:13.730
But I think it's important,

00:19:13.730 --> 00:19:16.040
but you can ask me more and I can try

00:19:16.040 --> 00:19:19.900
to guide if you have any
questions about the company.

00:19:19.900 --> 00:19:20.970
So what do they do?

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:21.981
The distribution company.

00:19:21.981 --> 00:19:23.937
And this is something actually that many

00:19:23.937 --> 00:19:26.470
of the other distribution
companies that we interview,

00:19:26.470 --> 00:19:28.250
they say they do is that they sub contract

00:19:28.250 --> 00:19:29.280
drivers and tracks.

00:19:29.280 --> 00:19:31.606
And they try to put very little

00:19:31.606 --> 00:19:34.233
of the company
identification in the track.

00:19:35.100 --> 00:19:36.922
And since El Salvador is small,

00:19:36.922 --> 00:19:40.080
what they do is the tracks
leave the work place

00:19:40.080 --> 00:19:42.310
and they return each day.

00:19:42.310 --> 00:19:45.600
So we have about 90,000 trips,

00:19:45.600 --> 00:19:48.923
more than 2 million deliveries
to retailers or pharmacies.

00:19:50.870 --> 00:19:53.020
So how does it work, the extortion?

00:19:53.020 --> 00:19:56.730
So this company, distribution
company in particular,

00:19:56.730 --> 00:19:58.090
and also the other ones,

00:19:58.090 --> 00:20:00.950
they have kind of their
own security policy.

00:20:00.950 --> 00:20:05.200
So they have a robust security
team that monitors each track

00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:07.020
and negotiate with the gangs.

00:20:07.020 --> 00:20:09.430
So this is super costly for the company

00:20:09.430 --> 00:20:12.500
'cause they have to have their
own security team inside.

00:20:12.500 --> 00:20:17.040
So how it works is that the
driver goes with the tracks,

00:20:17.040 --> 00:20:18.703
to go to the delivery.

00:20:18.703 --> 00:20:20.880
And prior to the delivery,

00:20:20.880 --> 00:20:24.370
someone that is a gang
representative collects extortion

00:20:24.370 --> 00:20:26.202
and ask for an extortion amount.

00:20:26.202 --> 00:20:28.140
What the driver has to do in that moment,

00:20:28.140 --> 00:20:31.130
he doesn't have to negotiate himself.

00:20:31.130 --> 00:20:34.890
He has to tell the person we
need to call the security team

00:20:34.890 --> 00:20:36.970
and they will negotiate with you.

00:20:36.970 --> 00:20:39.060
So he calls the security team,

00:20:39.060 --> 00:20:41.423
confirm the amount and
receipt of payments.

00:20:42.810 --> 00:20:45.520
In very few cases, at least
that we could see our data,

00:20:45.520 --> 00:20:48.640
the extortion amount is
prenegotiated for a given period

00:20:48.640 --> 00:20:50.363
like monthly or weekly.

00:20:51.720 --> 00:20:54.170
And we ask why they
were having this system.

00:20:54.170 --> 00:20:58.280
And instead of putting
security to these drivers,

00:20:58.280 --> 00:21:00.950
like a police officer there or something,

00:21:00.950 --> 00:21:03.330
and what they emphasize
is that this is to ensure

00:21:03.330 --> 00:21:06.570
safety of drivers and reduces
also fraud of the drivers.

00:21:06.570 --> 00:21:08.510
And that's why they do it this way.

00:21:08.510 --> 00:21:09.380
They said in the past,

00:21:09.380 --> 00:21:11.290
when they try to increase
security of the driver

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:13.490
to come with another like guard,

00:21:13.490 --> 00:21:15.313
this generated more problems.

00:21:16.870 --> 00:21:18.340
And you may be thinking,

00:21:18.340 --> 00:21:21.090
extortion is illegal
and this in El Salvador,

00:21:21.090 --> 00:21:23.500
but the distribution company
has reported extortion

00:21:23.500 --> 00:21:24.775
to the Attorney's General Office.

00:21:24.775 --> 00:21:26.605
So they have all this data.

00:21:26.605 --> 00:21:29.036
So they know that this is going on.

00:21:29.036 --> 00:21:30.495
So how does it look?

00:21:30.495 --> 00:21:31.650
This is a map of El Salvador,

00:21:31.650 --> 00:21:34.280
and here we have all
the extortion payments.

00:21:34.280 --> 00:21:39.280
As you can see, a lot of
places do extortion payments.

00:21:39.570 --> 00:21:43.230
These companies stop and pay extortion.

00:21:43.230 --> 00:21:45.640
And also there is a lot of variation

00:21:45.640 --> 00:21:46.940
on what they are paying.

00:21:46.940 --> 00:21:49.050
Sometimes it's something just to give you

00:21:49.050 --> 00:21:53.430
the exact numbers in the next
slide, something like 50 cents

00:21:53.430 --> 00:21:54.290
that you can pay.

00:21:54.290 --> 00:21:58.103
And something large amount, like $140.

00:21:59.780 --> 00:22:04.680
And the other track pays
extortion about $14 per route

00:22:04.680 --> 00:22:05.960
in a day,

00:22:05.960 --> 00:22:08.130
which can seem small
because we were like, oh,

00:22:08.130 --> 00:22:09.930
this is not that much when,

00:22:09.930 --> 00:22:12.820
but then when we compare it
with the cost, for instance,

00:22:12.820 --> 00:22:15.813
of the daily label cost of the truck,

00:22:15.813 --> 00:22:16.646
diver is not,

00:22:16.646 --> 00:22:17.780
it's actually kinda similar.

00:22:20.085 --> 00:22:24.720
- [Narrator] So the payments
are per trip or per day?

00:22:26.434 --> 00:22:28.590
- No, it's not per trip,

00:22:28.590 --> 00:22:31.823
it's actually it's per
delivery, the payments.

00:22:33.020 --> 00:22:33.853
Exactly.

00:22:33.853 --> 00:22:36.160
So every time it's not
that they negotiate,

00:22:36.160 --> 00:22:37.810
and this is something that we saw,

00:22:37.810 --> 00:22:40.760
it's not that they negotiate
a payment per route,

00:22:40.760 --> 00:22:43.570
these gangs, so they don't
act that centralized.

00:22:43.570 --> 00:22:45.440
Actually, we even check in the correlates,

00:22:45.440 --> 00:22:48.740
whether what you are
paying in the same route,

00:22:48.740 --> 00:22:51.050
that same route that driver is doing,

00:22:51.050 --> 00:22:53.541
whether the payment that he's
doing first is correlated

00:22:53.541 --> 00:22:56.240
with the extortion amount
of the other payments.

00:22:56.240 --> 00:22:58.120
And we don't see any correlation.

00:22:58.120 --> 00:23:01.810
So it's really related with
this local downstream demands

00:23:01.810 --> 00:23:04.150
with where is the place
where you are delivering,

00:23:04.150 --> 00:23:06.167
if it is a rich area or not.

00:23:09.880 --> 00:23:12.520
So we take all this data of extortion

00:23:12.520 --> 00:23:14.780
and we combined it also
with the sales data.

00:23:14.780 --> 00:23:16.053
And the first thing that
we wanted to do was,

00:23:16.053 --> 00:23:18.920
okay, let's see what
correlates with extortion,

00:23:18.920 --> 00:23:20.420
focusing on the nearest scale.

00:23:21.740 --> 00:23:23.900
And as I was just saying before to Teresa,

00:23:23.900 --> 00:23:25.370
what the first thing that we see

00:23:25.370 --> 00:23:27.420
is some evidence of price discrimination.

00:23:28.730 --> 00:23:31.920
So we see that the extortion
amount that they pay

00:23:31.920 --> 00:23:35.000
is increasing in the delivery, sorry.

00:23:35.000 --> 00:23:36.920
The value of goods per delivery,

00:23:36.920 --> 00:23:38.740
so it's positively correlated

00:23:38.740 --> 00:23:41.274
with the value of goods that you have

00:23:41.274 --> 00:23:42.370
when you are delivering.

00:23:42.370 --> 00:23:43.340
And interestingly,

00:23:43.340 --> 00:23:46.150
when we check with the
value of goods in track.

00:23:46.150 --> 00:23:47.450
So you may be thinking, well,

00:23:47.450 --> 00:23:48.490
maybe they're charging

00:23:48.490 --> 00:23:50.710
based on what they're carrying in track,

00:23:50.710 --> 00:23:53.742
but it's not that the
gangs take the effort

00:23:53.742 --> 00:23:55.700
to open the truck and try to see

00:23:55.700 --> 00:23:57.170
what they have inside, it's just,

00:23:57.170 --> 00:23:58.800
they know more is the value

00:23:58.800 --> 00:24:00.890
based on where you are delivering.

00:24:00.890 --> 00:24:03.220
So they know that you're going
to deliver to this pharmacy.

00:24:03.220 --> 00:24:04.860
We know that this pharmacy,

00:24:04.860 --> 00:24:08.020
it's in a rich area and
that's how they charge.

00:24:08.020 --> 00:24:10.520
And this is why we don't
see here any correlation.

00:24:12.139 --> 00:24:15.330
And this is what I was just saying before,

00:24:15.330 --> 00:24:17.150
because something we wanted to know was,

00:24:17.150 --> 00:24:20.290
is extortion the amount that they depend,

00:24:20.290 --> 00:24:22.554
does it depend on the number of stops

00:24:22.554 --> 00:24:26.040
along the same route that
these driver's doing,

00:24:26.040 --> 00:24:29.193
we don't see that much
areas of the correlation.

00:24:33.240 --> 00:24:35.300
We also try to see other measures

00:24:35.300 --> 00:24:37.580
and here's where we don't
have that much good data,

00:24:37.580 --> 00:24:39.090
because this is integrated.

00:24:39.090 --> 00:24:41.760
So we use this nightlight
density to try to see

00:24:41.760 --> 00:24:43.719
if it's possibly
correlated with extortion.

00:24:43.719 --> 00:24:46.189
And actually we see that's the case,

