we should see an increase in gang threats

00:37:45.960 --> 00:37:47.390
related to extortion.

00:37:47.390 --> 00:37:50.010
And also kidnapping is
something that happens

00:37:50.010 --> 00:37:54.230
or deprivation of liberty
is when I stop you

00:37:54.230 --> 00:37:55.157
for an amount of time,

00:37:55.157 --> 00:37:58.640
and I don't let you
move from that location,

00:37:58.640 --> 00:38:00.990
which is something that
happens a lot with drivers

00:38:00.990 --> 00:38:03.480
and with people when
they don't want to pay.

00:38:03.480 --> 00:38:05.530
And we actually see an increase of those.

00:38:06.480 --> 00:38:08.080
Then the other thing that,

00:38:08.080 --> 00:38:10.990
I don't know why it's not
showing here my click,

00:38:10.990 --> 00:38:13.804
but just stress me at this increase.

00:38:13.804 --> 00:38:16.670
And the second thing that we
were thinking that may happen

00:38:16.670 --> 00:38:20.570
is that the degree of the price
discrimination might change

00:38:20.570 --> 00:38:24.220
because now gangs may have
better information on retailers

00:38:24.220 --> 00:38:25.450
and associated demand
for the delivered goods.

00:38:25.450 --> 00:38:28.150
Since I'm not fighting,
now I can know better

00:38:28.150 --> 00:38:31.270
how much is the price of those goods

00:38:31.270 --> 00:38:33.790
that you're going to deliver and actually,

00:38:33.790 --> 00:38:35.670
we see some areas of that,

00:38:35.670 --> 00:38:38.200
we see that gangs increase extortion more

00:38:38.200 --> 00:38:40.440
for deliveries that advertise

00:38:40.440 --> 00:38:42.873
with higher value of delivery.

00:38:43.840 --> 00:38:45.553
And the third thing that we find is this,

00:38:45.553 --> 00:38:48.096
that I was talking before is that,

00:38:48.096 --> 00:38:50.500
if they're taking longer
time to negotiate,

00:38:50.500 --> 00:38:53.520
because now they have more
people there per stop,

00:38:53.520 --> 00:38:54.650
this should take longer.

00:38:54.650 --> 00:38:55.685
Now the delivery.

00:38:55.685 --> 00:38:59.005
And we actually see that an
increase in the delivery times

00:38:59.005 --> 00:39:01.353
between the extortion
payments and the delivery,

00:39:01.353 --> 00:39:04.600
consistent again with this
idea of more negotiations,

00:39:04.600 --> 00:39:07.353
negotiations and hold-up
by gangs after the pact.

00:39:09.180 --> 00:39:11.470
We also try to explore other explanations.

00:39:11.470 --> 00:39:12.303
As I was saying,

00:39:12.303 --> 00:39:14.320
this is just suggestiveness mechanism,

00:39:14.320 --> 00:39:15.317
we're working on this,

00:39:15.317 --> 00:39:17.256
and any feedback that you can give about

00:39:17.256 --> 00:39:20.180
how to try to strangle
these different mechanisms

00:39:20.180 --> 00:39:22.630
we were just discussing
before (indistinct), yes.

00:39:25.980 --> 00:39:28.495
- Given that you'll ask for the question,

00:39:28.495 --> 00:39:30.453
Ill do it.

00:39:31.610 --> 00:39:34.430
What do you mean by press
discrimination exactly?

00:39:34.430 --> 00:39:35.850
What do you have in mind?

00:39:35.850 --> 00:39:38.264
- Yes, basically,
whether they are charging

00:39:38.264 --> 00:39:40.340
a fixed fee per delivery,

00:39:40.340 --> 00:39:44.630
or if they are varying based
on the value of deliveries

00:39:44.630 --> 00:39:47.290
or they vary extortion amount

00:39:47.290 --> 00:39:49.703
based on where they are delivering.

00:39:51.229 --> 00:39:54.440
And this is what I'm seeing in
the data, what we are seeing.

00:39:56.150 --> 00:40:00.960
- Yeah, because again, I
think that data on the rates.

00:40:00.960 --> 00:40:05.153
So the ratio between the extortion amount.

00:40:05.153 --> 00:40:06.450
- How much it's from the vary.

00:40:06.450 --> 00:40:08.370
- It would be quite interesting here,

00:40:08.370 --> 00:40:12.473
because suppose that you
find it everywhere, like 10%.

00:40:16.970 --> 00:40:18.270
- Yes, so it is gone.

00:40:18.270 --> 00:40:20.420
- Yeah, there could be a situation

00:40:20.420 --> 00:40:24.010
where it's not 10% everywhere,

00:40:24.010 --> 00:40:28.360
but depending on, so yeah.

00:40:28.360 --> 00:40:32.273
Some sort of a socio demand
for the services, so to speak.

00:40:33.340 --> 00:40:35.840
Then you charge more or less.

00:40:35.840 --> 00:40:40.840
And that's what I interpret
as price discrimination.

00:40:41.111 --> 00:40:43.715
- Yeah, we should
definitely think of the rate

00:40:43.715 --> 00:40:47.770
that you suggested, Pamela.

00:40:47.770 --> 00:40:49.450
- Yeah, so do you, I mean,

00:40:49.450 --> 00:40:53.410
how should I think about any response

00:40:53.410 --> 00:40:56.670
in terms of the types of delivery
or the values of delivery,

00:40:56.670 --> 00:40:57.970
'cause that's also indulges, right?

00:40:57.970 --> 00:40:59.520
So there might be an adjustment

00:40:59.520 --> 00:41:04.520
in how much valuable am I
deciding to ship for every trip,

00:41:07.610 --> 00:41:11.050
because I know now that there
is going to be more extortion.

00:41:11.050 --> 00:41:12.180
- No, yes.

00:41:12.180 --> 00:41:13.220
That's very important.

00:41:13.220 --> 00:41:14.333
And actually we,

00:41:15.206 --> 00:41:18.003
this is actually, I think
it's the third bullet.

00:41:19.030 --> 00:41:20.770
So basically the firm can adjust.

00:41:20.770 --> 00:41:22.518
So once they are facing this face,

00:41:22.518 --> 00:41:25.268
this increasing extortion rates,

00:41:25.268 --> 00:41:27.280
they can just be a price searching

00:41:27.280 --> 00:41:31.530
like a higher delivery
fee to the retailers

00:41:31.530 --> 00:41:35.460
or to just not deliver,
or change the goods

00:41:35.460 --> 00:41:36.820
